# {{ title }}

A React Dart application with server-side rendering and server functions.

## Setup

```sh
dart pub get
```

## Build

```sh
dart run react_tool:react build
```

## Run

```sh
dart run react_tool:react serve
```

The server runs on `http://localhost:8080` and the SSR worker on port
`3001`. Server functions live in `lib/greeting.dart` and are called from
the browser through the generated client
(`lib/.generated/greeting.client.g.dart`).

## Test

```sh
# Fast unit tests (no build, uses react_testing harnesses)
dart test

# With coverage
dart run react_tool:react test --coverage
# or
dart test --coverage

# Full-stack SSR + server-function integration (builds + boots Node worker)
dart test -t integration
```

Tests use `react_testing`: `ServerFunctionHarness` for server functions,
`SsrTestHarness`/`InMemorySsrHarness` for SSR documents and
`ReactComponentHarness` for components. See `test/app_test.dart` and
`test/greeting_test.dart`.

## Analyze

```sh
dart run react_tool:react analyze
# verbose
dart run react_tool:react analyze --verbose
```

Uses `react_analysis` for component, hook and SSR diagnostics (same engine as the IDE plugin). Run `dart run react_tool:react doctor` to check setup.

## Docker

The multi-stage `Dockerfile` builds the server binary and JS bundles in
stage 1 and runs them in a slim Node runtime. Build it from the workspace
root so the context includes the `packages/` directory:

```sh
docker build -f {{ name }}/Dockerfile .
```
